    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6214" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνα</span></b>  (A), [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰνᾰ</span>],
		voc. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄναξ,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>king,</i> only in the phrases
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦ ἄνα,</span>
			
				contr.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦνα,</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ζεῦ ἄνα,</span> and always as address to gods: fem., 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦ ἄνασσα</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				12.3
			</span></i>: ult. elided only in <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Ap.</u>
				526
			</span></i> codd.—
				Ep.
			, Lyr., and occasionally Trag., as <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				1485
			</span></i> (lyr.).</div>
